-- Story 18.1 fixtures: mill/year contexts for the two admin reversals on the Schedules 1-10
-- track -- Set to Draft (S->D, UC-CHK-016) and Set to Submit (V->S, UC-CHK-018).
--
-- PREFIX IS DELIBERATE, and for the reason R__55 records. This must sort BELOW
-- R__70_test_scope_canonical_submitter.sql, which associates the canonical submitter set-based
-- over every ILCR_MILL_STATUS_XREF row that exists when it runs. A prefix above 70 would leave
-- these mills outside submitter scope, and SetReportStatusAuthorizationIT's submitter-refused
-- arm would then pass for the WRONG reason -- out of scope rather than lacking the action.
--
-- GUARDED INSERTS, unlike R__55's. Every statement is a single-row SELECT ... FROM DUAL behind
-- WHERE NOT EXISTS on its own PK (the R__51:106-114 idiom). A multi-row UNION ALL would break
-- ci-seed-parity.setup.ts, and the guard's job is to keep a checksum change from failing the
-- migration rather than to make a dirty container clean.
--
-- MILLS ARE CLASS-OWNED, NOT SHARED. A successful reversal genuinely mutates: it moves the
-- track status, ten category rows and the audit columns of thirteen tables. The four mills that
-- succeed or roll back (790/791/795/798) are each written by exactly one test; the refused and
-- closed mills (792/793/794/796/797) are never written at all, by construction. Nothing here
-- touches 514/530/601/617 (CheckStatusSweepIT fingerprints those) or 764-770 (R__55's).
--
-- SCHEDULE 11 IS SEEDED TO A DIFFERENT CODE ON EVERY ROW (AC 11). Each 1-10 track is paired
-- with MILL_SILVICULTUR_STATUS_CODE 'V' where the 1-10 code is not 'V', and 'D' where it is, so
-- a write that reached the wrong column fails the test instead of passing by coincidence.
--
-- BOTH IDENTITY PAIRS ARE SEEDED NON-NULL (AC 3). LICENSEE_MILL_ID/LICENSEE_USER_GUID and
-- AUDITOR_MILL_ID/AUDITOR_USER_GUID carry known values on every mill, so the ITs can assert the
-- reversals leave them UNCHANGED BY VALUE rather than merely non-null -- the assertion that
-- actually distinguishes D1's ruling from the wrong SET list. The GUIDs reference the two
-- canonical xref users; the mill ids are the mills' own, matching the composite FKs
-- V20260915 declared.
--
-- CATEGORY SEED STATES follow the pair legacy would really have left behind: 'A' for a
-- Submitted track (submit runs D->A) and 'V' for a Verified one (S->V runs A->V). Set to Draft
-- writes A->D and Set to Submit writes V->A, so the seeds are what those transitions actually
-- start from.
--
-- All-met data is seeded for Schedules 1, 2 and 3 only, cloned statement-for-statement from
-- R__55's mill 764. The other eight schedules on the track report zero rows as a vacuous MET, so
-- no data is needed to make the gate pass.
--
-- No ILCR_MILL_REPORT_STATUS_RPT_VW rows: MillReportStatusIT asserts exactly five 2021 rows.
--
-- ID blocks claimed: MILL_ID 790-799, ILCR_REPORT_SUMMARY_ID 1650-1699 (of which 1690-1691 are
-- BASIC_SILVICULTURE_REPORT_ID, a different table sharing the claimed band), ILCR_COST_REPORT_DETAIL_ID
-- 3201-3500. Re-grepped across db/ AND db-e2e/ immediately before commit: zero occurrences of any
-- integer in those three bands, WITH db/README.md's db-e2e reservations (summaries 3001-3199,
-- cost details 4001-4499, transportation 4801-4899) excluded by hand -- the README states those
-- as range strings, so a token scan of the SQL does not see them. That re-grep is not optional
-- and not once: 15.3 lost its block to Epic 21 between drafting and merge, and both files'
-- WHERE NOT EXISTS guards would have let Flyway apply both silently rather than raising
-- ORA-00001.
--
-- THE COST-DETAIL BLOCK MUST STAY BELOW 9000, and this is the second constraint, not a
-- restatement of the first. V4 creates THE.ILCR_COST_REPORT_DETAIL_SEQ and V20260811 re-creates
-- it START WITH 10000; every cost-line write in the suite draws NEXTVAL from it. This block was
-- first claimed at 10500-10751 -- unused by any fixture, and therefore 'free' by the usual
-- check -- and a full run climbed the sequence into it. The result was 38 IT failures as bare
-- 500s on Schedules 3/4/6/7A/10 write paths, none of them reproducible in a single-class run,
-- and none of them mentioning this file. A static id is only free if it is out of reach of
-- every sequence as well as every other fixture.

-- The two directory identities the seeded identity pairs point at. They exist ONLY so those
-- pairs can be non-null: V20260915's ILCR_IMUX_LICENSEE_FK / ILCR_IMUX_AUDITOR_FK are composite
-- FKs onto ILCR_MILL_USER_XREF (ILCR_MILL_ID, USER_GUID), so a status row naming a pair with no
-- xref row fails at Flyway boot. R__70's canonical submitter cannot serve: it sorts AFTER this
-- file, so its xref rows do not exist yet when these status rows are inserted.
--
-- Neither identity is ever the ACTING user in a test. The reversals record no one (D1), so an
-- acting-user association would prove nothing; what these rows buy is the ability to assert the
-- four columns are unchanged BY VALUE after a reversal, which is the only assertion that tells
-- D1's ruling apart from a wrong SET list. A 'not null' assertion would pass against the auditor
-- statement too.
INSERT INTO THE.ILCR_USER (USER_GUID, ILCR_ROLE_NAME, ACTIVE_IND, REVISION_COUNT, ENTRY_USERID, ENTRY_TIMESTAMP, UPDATE_USERID, UPDATE_TIMESTAMP)
  SELECT 'REVERSALLICENSEE1111222233334444', 'LICENSEE', 'Y', 0, 'SEED', SYSDATE, 'SEED', SYSDATE FROM DUAL
   WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM THE.ILCR_USER WHERE USER_GUID = 'REVERSALLICENSEE1111222233334444');
INSERT INTO THE.ILCR_USER (USER_GUID, ILCR_ROLE_NAME, ACTIVE_IND, REVISION_COUNT, ENTRY_USERID, ENTRY_TIMESTAMP, UPDATE_USERID, UPDATE_TIMESTAMP)
  SELECT 'REVERSALAUDITOR11111222233334444', 'ADMIN', 'Y', 0, 'SEED', SYSDATE, 'SEED', SYSDATE FROM DUAL
   WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM THE.ILCR_USER WHERE USER_GUID = 'REVERSALAUDITOR11111222233334444');

